"body": "A simple baseline for regression is to always predict the same value, regardless of the input features. The most common choice is the average of the training targets.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nIn the plot, each dot is a target value from a small illustrative set. The horizontal line shows the constant prediction equal to the mean (27). Because the line ignores the input, the error for each point is simply the distance from its dot to the line.\n\nUsing the mean minimizes the sum of squared errors across the training data, making it the optimal constant predictor under the usual $L_2$ loss. It provides a reference point: any model must beat this baseline to be useful.",
