"body": "Consider the token “sat” as the query in a self‑attention layer. It looks at every token, assigning a numeric weight to each.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nThe largest weight (0.75) goes to the final token “mat”, meaning the model links “sat” most strongly to the action’s object. Smaller weights spread to the surrounding words, with “cat” receiving 0.10.\n\nThese weights illustrate how attention captures syntactic relations: the verb focuses on its complement while still acknowledging the subject and prepositions.\n\nIn practice, the sum of all weights equals 1, so the distribution reflects relative importance rather than absolute scores.",
